  A +7 elven shield gives 9 AC.  (That's the equivalent of another +0
suit of Dragon Scale Mail in protection.)  

  Given the way damage reduction works at AC below zero that should save
about 4 HP per damaging hit.  That can be important when mobbed,
especially in a summoning storm.  Worst/best case: 8 * 4.5 = 36 HP per
turn.  (Might even be useful vs Air Elementals, they seem to get in
multiple attacks a lot.)

  Elven armor can be safely enchanted at +5.  

  An elven shield weighs 40.
  A small shield weighs 30.

  Downside: Elven shields cut spell casting success rates by 3/4.  Small
shields don't.  OTOH it's easy to 'T'ake off a shield, cast a spell,
then 'W'ear the shield again.

  Note that #twoweaponing/shield is not an absolute choice.  #twoweapon
in the mazes, etc.  Wear a shield and zap wands of teleport in the
Endgame.


